{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733828",
      "title": "Routing: Multiple Pages in Single-Page Applications",
      "sourceHash": "aa4ebb8f91fc523da76355e20105525258b7f0e9fc45e60c12356f666e9ddbce",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "Now before we write any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "or install any package, let me again clarify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 10.68,
          "en": "what exactly Routing is and why it matters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.68,
          "end": 13.98,
          "en": "and why we might want to add it to our website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.98,
          "end": 17.67,
          "en": "And to understand Routing, it's important to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.67,
          "end": 20.31,
          "en": "how the web generally works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.31,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "When you visit websites you can typically append a path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "after the domain name like, slash Welcome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 32.13,
          "en": "and that loads, for example, the welcome page of a website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.13,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "And if you then type a different URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "into the browser address bar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 39.69,
          "en": "or if you click a link that changes the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.69,
          "end": 41.82,
          "en": "for example, to slash Products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 43.59,
          "en": "a different page gets loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 47.49,
          "en": "So the visible content of the website changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 49.32,
          "en": "That's what Routing is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 54.32,
          "en": "Different URL paths load different content on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.54,
          "end": 56.82,
          "en": "and that's what we didn't have up to this point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.82,
          "end": 59.37,
          "en": "in the applications we built in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.37,
          "end": 61.83,
          "en": "because there we never had an opportunity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.83,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "of changing the URL or reacting to different URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 69.81,
          "en": "and loading different content based on the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 73.23,
          "en": "That's what will change in this course section though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "Now, traditionally, you would implement Routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 78.63,
          "en": "by simply loading different content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.63,
          "end": 82.56,
          "en": "different HTML files for different paths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.56,
          "end": 86.01,
          "en": "and that is how you would build a multi-page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.01,
          "end": 89.43299999999999,
          "en": "which you typically would build without ReactJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.42,
          "end": 92.55,
          "en": "Now, with that, you get different content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.55,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "for different paths, but the disadvantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 98.16,
          "en": "is that you always have to fetch new content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.16,
          "end": 102.36,
          "en": "A new HTTP request is sent and a new response is received,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 105.81,
          "en": "and that can kind of break the user flow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.81,
          "end": 109.25999999999999,
          "en": "It can introduce some lag and slow down your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 114,
          "en": "and it can therefore lead to a suboptimal user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114,
          "end": 116.955,
          "en": "So that's why we might wanna build a single page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.955,
          "end": 120.9,
          "en": "when we're building more complex user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.9,
          "end": 124.29,
          "en": "With those, you send only one initial HTML request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.29,
          "end": 128.73,
          "en": "and then this HTML file with a bunch of extra JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.73,
          "end": 132.21,
          "en": "is downloaded, and thereafter the extra JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 134.85,
          "en": "that runs on the client will actually take care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.85,
          "end": 137.64,
          "en": "about adjusting what the user sees on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.64,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "That's how single page applications work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 143.19,
          "en": "However, that does not mean that we can't bring back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.19,
          "end": 144.54,
          "en": "the illusion of a Routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 148.38,
          "en": "and that we can support path changes in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.38,
          "end": 151.71,
          "en": "and load different content based on the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.71,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "Instead, we can add client-side React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 158.67000000000002,
          "en": "that basically watches the currently active URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.67000000000002,
          "end": 161.73,
          "en": "and that triggers whenever the URL changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.73,
          "end": 164.79,
          "en": "and that then leads to different content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.79,
          "end": 168.81,
          "en": "being displayed on the screen when the URL changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.81,
          "end": 172.02,
          "en": "So instead of loading new HTML files from the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.02,
          "end": 173.97,
          "en": "we could add some client-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.97,
          "end": 176.64,
          "en": "that simply watches the URL and then loads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.64,
          "end": 180.81,
          "en": "a different React component when that URL changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.81,
          "end": 183.66,
          "en": "With that, we're still in a single page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 183.66,
          "end": 186.87,
          "en": "but we nonetheless support different URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "and therefore Routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 190.08,
          "en": "And that is exactly what we'll do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.08,
          "end": 193.293,
          "en": "and what we will learn about in this course section here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}